From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 3 AVPs from 3GPP TS 29.389
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3GPP TS 29.389 V18.0.0 defines these AVPs in vendor 10415, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  V2X-Authorization-Data (4700): Grouped, 3 members, clause 6.3.2
  V2X-Permission-in-VPLMN (4701): Unsigned32, clause 6.3.3
  V2X-Application-Server (4702): Grouped, 2 members, clause 6.3.4

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

The document states no flag rules for V2X-Authorization-Data,
V2X-Permission-in-VPLMN, V2X-Application-Server, so their mandatory
attribute is left at the dictionary's default, and the V bit follows the
Vendor-ID (RFC 6733 section 4.1).

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..55d3199 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -8939,6 +8939,22 @@
 		<avp name="FE-Identifier-List" code="4413" mandatory="must" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" protected="may" vendor-id="TGPP">
 			<type type-name="UTF8String"/>
 		</avp>
+		<avp name="V2X-Authorization-Data" code="4700" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<grouped>
+				<gavp name="V2X-Permission-in-VPLMN"/>
+				<gavp name="PC5-RAT-Type"/>
+				<gavp name="V2X-Application-Server"/>
+			</grouped>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="V2X-Permission-in-VPLMN" code="4701" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+		</avp>
+		<avp name="V2X-Application-Server" code="4702" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="TGPP">
+			<grouped>
+				<gavp name="Application-Server"/>
+				<gavp name="Geographical-Information"/>
+			</grouped>
+		</avp>
 		<!--
 		Note: The AVP codes from 4400 to 4499 are reserved for TS 32.299
 		-->
